# `vite.config.ts` applies the desktop default (see `DEFAULT_ACCOUNTS_API`), so
# a plain `pnpm build` needs nothing here. Copy this file to `.env.local`
# (gitignored, applied before Vite reads it) or export the variable before
# `pnpm build` to point this app at another account service. Baked at build
# time; an explicitly empty value means "same origin as this page", which this
# app cannot sign in from — it then reports the missing account service instead
# of navigating.
#
# The same default applies to `vite dev` and `vite preview`, so a sign-in from
# the desktop dev server reaches the production account service. Point them at
# another service with this file (`.env.local`) or an exported value; an
# explicit empty value shows the "not configured" notice locally.
VITE_ACCOUNTS_API=https://sciencediscovery.openjiuwen.com/accounts

# Read at runtime by the local API the desktop shell starts, to verify account
# tokens on the loopback bootstrap route. The shell forwards its own value and
# falls back to the same public URL when it is unset; set an empty value to
# disable sign-in.
# SCIENCE_AGENT_ACCOUNTS_URL=https://sciencediscovery.openjiuwen.com/accounts
